# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values from your own Supabase
# project (Project Settings -> API) to enable the Supabase-backed live
# scheme-retrieval layer. Both variables are OPTIONAL — with neither set, the
# app runs exactly as it always has: the curated local scheme dataset only,
# no Supabase, no live retrieval, no errors.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is Supabase's public "anon" key, not a secret — it is
# safe to ship in browser code by design and is constrained server-side by Row
# Level Security. Never put a Supabase SERVICE ROLE key here or in any
# VITE_-prefixed variable — that key must only ever live in Supabase Edge
# Function secrets (set via `supabase secrets set`), never in this file or in
# frontend code.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The following are NOT read by the frontend and are not VITE_-prefixed on
# purpose. They configure the live-retrieval Edge Function
# (supabase/functions/live-scheme-retrieval) and must be set as Supabase
# secrets on your project, e.g.:
#   supabase secrets set DATA_GOV_IN_API_KEY=your-key-here
#   supabase secrets set DATA_GOV_IN_RESOURCE_ID=your-resource-id-here
# Get a free API key by registering at https://data.gov.in/user/register.
# See README.md for what this key does and does not enable.
# DATA_GOV_IN_API_KEY=
# DATA_GOV_IN_RESOURCE_ID=

# URL of a developer-run relay/proxy for Gemini Live voice — NOT a Gemini API
# key. Safe to expose in the browser: it is just an endpoint address, the same
# way VITE_SUPABASE_URL is safe. OPTIONAL — with it unset (the default), the
# app runs exactly as before: the Gemini Live voice provider correctly
# reports itself unavailable, no crash, no fake "connected" state. This repo
# does not ship the actual relay/proxy backend — see
# docs/voice-session-architecture.md and src/assistant/voice/geminiLiveConfig.ts
# for the two supported backend patterns and why a raw Gemini API key must
# NEVER go in this file or anywhere else browser-reachable.
# VITE_GEMINI_LIVE_PROXY_URL=
